    "supports": [
      "All four N5 models have 201 logged curve points from update 1 through update 20000, with finite losses and gradients and decreasing block-average training loss. These are training curves, not validation loss curves.",
      "Every method succeeds on 10/10 IID and 20/20 C development episodes. On E, B0 and P2 succeed on 0/20, while P1 and P3 succeed on 15/20. Thus this packet supports a substantial N5 development benefit for the existing cabinet-frame mechanism and no observed E success-rate gain from the joint future-geometry objective.",
      "B0 and P2 never reach within 5 cm of the interaction point on any E episode; P2 additionally has 11 recorded joint-violation episodes. P1 and P3 reach within 5 cm on every E episode, and their five failures each receive the descriptive near_handle_goal_not_completed label.",
      "P1 and P3 have four overlapping E failures and one exchanged success/failure: P1 alone fails E_009 and P3 alone fails E_015. P3 has a smaller mean minimum goal-point distance on E (0.04129 m versus 0.06083 m) but nearly equal mean final distance (0.07970 m versus 0.07927 m), and longer mean successful-episode duration (194.6 versus 179.6 steps). These are descriptive differences, not a demonstrated superiority.",
      "All eight real simulator frames depict the same successful C episode: four step-50 views near the handle and four terminal views with the door open. They visually support successful approach/opening in that selected case only."
    ]
